  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Labour market and employment policies and support to MSMEs in Kiribati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO has been supporting the development of Kiribati&apos;s first-ever National Employment Policy (NEP)&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201d; a coherent, comprehensive and integrated framework that promotes full and productive employment and decent work for all, in line with the SDGs. The NEP mainstreams employment in national policy-making and strives to achieve a dynamic and inclusive labour market by promoting job creation, enhancing skills development, and ensuring that employment opportunities are available and accessible to all.&#xc2;&#xa0;
The NEP was launched in December 2025 and support is required to facilitate its effective implementation. The priority areas include enhancing skills development, promoting employment in public and private sectors and improving working conditions across all sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
